{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528120580,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb0d53ffeBaw5RhZ4h4KChT","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2360ebe002mJpX2MEpnVZCXo","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb0d53ffeBaw5RhZ4h4KChT","messageID":"msg_1d235fd85001J1pcKo5QEmJMWV","type":"tool","id":"call_d57e4d0858e44e5f9f4495f0","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"DSH|dsh","path":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references","limit":20},"output":"Found 3 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/save-workflow.md:\n  Line 265: | `runtime` | string | `claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `devin` or `dsh`. `cursor` is accepted but not minted while its trigger stays gated. |\n\n  Line 269: | `locatorKind` | string | `transcript_path` for Claude and Codex, `live_branch_or_session_log` for Pi, `transcript_file` for Devin, `session_log` for DSH and `session-store` for OpenCode. |\n\n  Line 279: - **Sweep commands by runtime:** On Claude, `.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-transcript.mjs` prints the answers waiting for a record, each with its `sourceKey`. On OpenCode, Devin, Codex, Pi and DSH, `sweep-opencode.mjs`, `sweep-devin.mjs`, `sweep-codex.mjs`, `sweep-pi.mjs` and `sweep-dsh.mjs` in the same folder do the same from the runtime's stored session. The DSH sweep reads the session log under `$DSH_HOME/sessions`, or `~/.dsh/sessions` when `DSH_HOME` is unset, and also recovers a late reply to a timed question. Every sweep also prints chat candidates, through the shared detector in `lib/chat-questions.mjs`.\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":3,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 3 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/save-workflow.md:\n  Line 265: | `runtime` | string | `claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `devin` or `dsh`. `cursor` is accepted but not minted while its trigger stays gated. |\n\n  Line 269: | `locatorKind` | string | `transcript_path` for Claude and Codex, `live_branch_or_session_log` for Pi, `transcript_file` for Devin, `session_log` for DSH and `session-store` for OpenCode. |\n\n  Line 279: - **Sweep commands by runtime:** On Claude, `.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-transcript.mjs` prints the answers waiting for a record, each with its `sourceKey`. On OpenCode, Devin, Codex, Pi and DSH, `sweep-opencode.mjs`, `sweep-devin.mjs`, `sweep-codex.mjs`, `sweep-pi.mjs` and `sweep-dsh.mjs` in the same folder do the same from the runtime's stored session. The DSH sweep reads the session log under `$DSH_HOME/sessions`, or `~/.dsh/sessions` when `DSH_HOME` is unset, and also recovers a late reply to a timed question. Every sweep also prints chat candidates, through the shared detector in `lib/chat-questions.mjs`.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"pattern\":\"DSH|dsh\",\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references\",\"limit\":20}"},"time":{"start":1794528120510,"end":1794528120580}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528120623,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb0d53ffeBaw5RhZ4h4KChT","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2360ec40019GDnRyIY8FeLm5","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb0d53ffeBaw5RhZ4h4KChT","messageID":"msg_1d235fd85001J1pcKo5QEmJMWV","type":"tool","id":"call_6ecfa8c451ed4cd299732018","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"hyphen","path":".","include":"*.md","limit":30},"output":"Found 30 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/README.md:\n  Line 208: Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/speckit-complete`. Devin reaches the same workflow through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md:\n  Line 65: Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-git/README.md:\n  Line 298: | Skill packaging and structure | `python3 .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/package_skill.py .skilled/skills/sk-git --check` reports `PASS` (snake_case findings on `references/`/`assets/` are advisory ahead of the hyphen-naming program) |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v3+/v3.4.0.0.md:\n  Line 168: The new phrase routes cover identifiers that were going unrouted. A new inline comment warns future contributors not to put multi-word or hyphenated keys into the wrong dict.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-git/manual-testing-playbook/owner-first-worktree-tooling/owner-slug-branch-pair-validation.md:\n  Line 30: - Expected execution process: Run `validate-slug` against a clean kebab slug and slugs with underscores/leading/trailing/double hyphens; `validate-nnn` against 001..999 and 000/2-digit/4-digit values; `validate-branch` against a conformant `worktrees/NNN-slug`, a `branches/NNN-slug`, `main`, a release branch, a `backup/*` safety ref, and an owner-first legacy name; `validate-pair` against a matching and a mismatched branch/directory combination.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v3+/v3.5.0.3.md:\n  Line 25: - **Every README follows the same voice rules.** None carries em dashes, double-hyphen separators, semicolons, Oxford-comma lists or filler words.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v3+/v3.5.0.4.md:\n  Line 166: The comment-hygiene checker grew the patterns it was missing. It now catches RC, single-number DR, hyphen phase and council-seat labels, and it scans inline trailing comments rather than only full-line ones. A blanket F-number pattern stayed out by design, because almost all of its matches are function keys and figures.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-ci-scaffold.md:\n  Line 64: Step 7 shows which refusal wins when a name is both protected and present, because the route resolves the target in a fixed order. `trigger-index-rebuild.yml` prints `REFUSE: trigger-index-rebuild.yml is a protected workflow`, not the existing-path line, since the protected list is checked before the filesystem. The second run prints `REFUSE: Probe_Check.yml is not a bare lowercase hyphen-case name ending in .yml`. Each run ends with `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"refused\"` and shows no plan.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.3.0.0.md:\n  Line 22: - **Playbook paths match the on-disk layout.** `SKILL.md` and `README` described scenario files using `manual-testing-playbook/<NN>--<topic>/<NNN>-<scenario>.md`. The actual layout is `manual-testing-playbook/<topic>/<scenario>.md`, with `underscore_case` categories and no numeric prefixes. The root playbook's package-artifacts list and Section 15 cross-reference index had stale hyphenated paths for the existing `GIT-001`..`GIT-022` scenarios and now match their on-disk `underscore_case` names.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.3.2.0.md:\n  Line 3: description: \"v1.3.2.0 refreshes the sk-git documentation and moves its resource trees to hyphen-case names.\"\n\n  Line 14: v1.3.2.0 refreshes the sk-git documentation and moves its resource trees to hyphen-case names. Script behavior, branch grammar and command surface did not change.\n\n  Line 22: - **Four resource trees now use hyphen-case names.** Their path references were repointed to match.\n\n  Line 32: `references/`, `assets/`, `feature-catalog/` and `manual-testing-playbook/` replaced their snake_case names with hyphen-case names. The move covered 66 files and 13 directories. Every path reference was repointed. This included the Smart Router's `RESOURCE_MAP`, `LOADING_LEVELS` and `DEFAULT_RESOURCE`. Relative cross-links, link labels and per-feature metadata also use the new names. Findings from `package_skill.py --check` for snake_case in `references/` and `assets/` are advisory-only until the repo-wide naming program flips the checker.\n\n  Line 60: - Any external reference to a sk-git resource path should use the hyphen-case name.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/worktree-naming/owner-first-worktree-naming.md:\n  Line 27: A legal branch is one of several shapes: `main` (reserved), a `skilled/vA.B.C.D` release branch, a `worktrees/NNN-slug` task branch, or a `branches/NNN-slug` dedicated branch. The slug is lowercase kebab-case with no leading, trailing, or doubled hyphen; the number is exactly 3 digits with value 001..999 interpreted base-10. `is_valid_pair` cross-checks that a `worktrees/NNN-slug` branch and a `.worktrees/NNN-slug` directory actually agree with each other — a branch `worktrees/0041-fix-thing` must pair with `.worktrees/0041-fix-thing`, not any other basename. Two legal-but-not-task lanes stay distinct: the launch-wrapper lane (`work/<runtime>/<slug>`, recognized by `is_wrapper_branch`) and safety refs (`backup/<anything>`, recognized by `is_backup_branch`), so callers can tell \"exempt lane\" apart from \"malformed.\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/sk-git/z_archive/002-sk-git-superset-worktrees/spec.md:\n  Line 124: | REQ-003 | Branch name sanitization pipeline | Documentation includes sanitize (lowercase, hyphens), truncate (max 100 chars), deduplicate steps |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/sk-git/z_archive/002-sk-git-superset-worktrees/plan.md:\n  Line 142:   3. Sanitize branch name (lowercase → hyphens → truncate → dedup)\n\n  Line 512: **Context**: Superset sanitizes branch names through a multi-step pipeline (lowercase, hyphens, truncate, dedup). sk-git uses simple `type/description` convention with no sanitization.\n\n  Line 514: **Decision**: Adopt a simplified sanitization pipeline using shell commands: sanitize (lowercase, hyphens, remove invalid chars) → truncate (100 char max) → dedup (append -1, -2 suffix if exists). Always show the sanitized name to the user before proceeding.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/sk-git/z_archive/013-git-review-remediation/spec.md:\n  Line 3: description: \"Close the two open GPT-5.6-sol review items on sk-git: (1) add a Git Workspace Safety subsection to AGENTS.md (ask-first worktree rule, owner-first grammar, forbidden branch commands, hyphen-pilot guard) plus a quick-ref row update; and (2) five pre-existing findings — a test-harness mktemp guard (cd \\\"\\\" returns 0), a >9999 allocator-exhaustion guard, catalog<->references contract reconciliation, SKILL.md NEVER safety refusals, and a cross-skill sk-doc validate_document.py fix (hyphen doc-type detection + CLI --type).\"\n\n  Line 54: | **Source** | GPT-5.6-sol review of packet `012-readme-enrichment-and-hyphen-naming` |\n\n  Line 66: 1. **AGENTS.md has no Git Workspace Safety guidance.** The Mandatory Tools table names `Git (sk-git)` but an agent that reads only `AGENTS.md` (not the full `SKILL.md`) has no summary of the ask-first worktree-vs-branch rule, the owner-first branch grammar, the allocate-never-count discipline, the forbidden `git branch` / `checkout -b` / `switch -c` commands, or the standing \"do not revert the sk-git hyphen pilot to snake_case\" guard.\n\n  Line 73:    - **2e — cross-skill sk-doc validator.** `sk-doc/shared/scripts/validate_document.py` detects `playbook_feature` / `feature_catalog` doc types only by underscore path tokens (`/manual_testing_playbook/`, `/feature_catalog/`), so after sk-git's hyphen rename those leaves fall through to `readme`; and the CLI `--type` choices omit `playbook`, `playbook_feature`, and `feature_catalog` even though all three are valid `documentTypes`.\n\n  Line 93: - **`.opencode/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/validate_document.py`** (cross-skill): teach hyphen + underscore doc-type detection; expose `playbook`/`playbook_feature`/`feature_catalog` via CLI `--type`.\n\n  Line 124: | REQ-001 | AGENTS.md carries a Git Workspace Safety subsection | Subsection appears after the Mandatory Tools table; covers ask-first worktree rule, owner-first `{owner}/{NNNN}-{slug}` grammar, allocate-never-count via `worktree-naming.sh`, forbidden `git branch`/`checkout -b`/`switch -c`, and the hyphen-pilot guard; the Git-workflow quick-ref row is updated to point at it |\n\n  Line 129: | REQ-006 | The sk-doc validator classifies hyphen-named playbook/catalog leaves and exposes them via CLI | `detect_document_type` returns `playbook_feature`/`feature_catalog` for both hyphen and underscore dir names; CLI `--type` accepts `playbook`, `playbook_feature`, `feature_catalog`; the `template_rules.json` path is left unchanged (already correct) |\n\n  Line 142: - **SC-006**: `validate_document.py` detects hyphen-named leaves + CLI `--type` exposes the three types; a hyphen-named playbook/catalog leaf classifies correctly.\n\n  Line 153: | Risk | Editing `validate_document.py` (cross-skill, shared by all skills) could regress other doc types | High | Change only the two additive detection lines + the CLI choices; run the sk-doc validator on existing readme/skill/spec docs to confirm no regression; verify a hyphen leaf classifies correctly |\n\n  Line 173: - A hyphen-named `feature-catalog/<category>/<feature>.md` and its underscore historical form must both classify as `feature_catalog`.\n\n  Line 195: - Prior packet: `../012-readme-enrichment-and-hyphen-naming/`\n\n\n(Results are truncated: showing first 30 results. Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":30,"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 30 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/README.md:\n  Line 208: Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/speckit-complete`. Devin reaches the same workflow through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md:\n  Line 65: Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-git/README.md:\n  Line 298: | Skill packaging and structure | `python3 .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/package_skill.py .skilled/skills/sk-git --check` reports `PASS` (snake_case findings on `references/`/`assets/` are advisory ahead of the hyphen-nam